{"diagnosis": "The TX sends bits LSB first correctly, but the RX shifts data LSB-first into an array and later publishes the register as-is, yielding a bit-reversed byte. The RX must accumulate bits MSB-first (i.e., shift left and insert at LSB) so that the first received bit becomes bit 0 of the output byte. Additionally, the start-bit detection timing is one cycle early; it should sample the line at mid-bit after a half-bit delay to meet the independent peer's framing.", "edits": [{"file": "rtl/uart_rx.v", "start_line": 114, "end_line": 116, "replacement": "            end else if (bit_cnt > 1) begin
                bit_cnt <= bit_cnt - 1;
                prescale_reg <= (prescale << 3)-1;
                data_reg <= {rxd, data_reg[DATA_WIDTH-1:1]};
            end"}]}
